WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:03.440
(singer singing in foreign language)

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.990
- [Narrator] People dancing
shoulder to shoulder

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:07.902
while listening to live
music in a stadium.

00:00:07.902 --> 00:00:09.600
(upbeat music)
(crowd clapping)

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.850
During the pandemic, scenes
like these have been rare

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.100
to say the least.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.090
- Wow, it's great, it feels great.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.070
Back to life.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.260
- [Narrator] 500 people were
able to attend this event

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.320
in Tel Aviv as long as they could prove

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.250
that they had been
vaccinated against COVID

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.483
by showing a QR code and an ID.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.730
It's part of a so-called
green pass system,

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.310
which is also accepted by gyms,

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:32.260
museums, bars and restaurants

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.760
as authorities want to demonstrate

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.540
that getting COVID shots gives access

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.140
to gatherings and public events.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.730
As of early March, more than
half of Israel's population

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.410
had received at least
one dose of the vaccine,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.450
a greater share than any other country.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.380
But a recent survey found
that 25% of Israelis

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.453
had no plans to take the vaccine.

00:00:51.414 --> 00:00:53.460
- Did you guys get vaccinated?

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.673
- [Narrator] To convince them, volunteers

00:00:54.673 --> 00:00:55.960
have been walking around

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.460
and touting the benefits of immunization.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.180
And health workers are offering freebies

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.870
that include free drinks, pizza

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.370
and tickets to basketball games

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:05.140
for those that get the vaccine.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.770
- If everybody will take the vaccine,

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.480
we can open all the stores,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.310
we can open all the business

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.960
and it's very important for the economy.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.590
- [Narrator] Israel is going to extremes

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.400
to reach its goal of
vaccinating everyone over 16

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.690
by the end of March and reopen its economy

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.273
as quickly as possible.

00:01:22.975 --> 00:01:24.090
(whistle blowing)

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.850
- Today we are spreading awareness

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.620
for everybody to get vaccines.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.830
- [Narrator] Ali Greenfield
is a volunteer medic.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.250
At this market in Jerusalem,

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.470
she helps spread the word

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.360
by encouraging people to get vaccinated

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.640
at a nearby bar where other volunteers

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.577
were also offering drinks.

00:01:38.577 --> 00:01:39.960
- The idea here is for
them to come to the bar,

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.100
they'll then receive a drink,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.088
a non-alcoholic drink

00:01:42.088 --> 00:01:43.824
in return for getting vaccinated.

00:01:43.824 --> 00:01:45.511
There you go.

00:01:45.511 --> 00:01:46.344
- [Narrator] By early March,

00:01:46.344 --> 00:01:48.280
the majority of people aged 50 and above

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:49.520
had been fully vaccinated

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.980
while less than half of
the population under 40

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:53.870
had received their first dose.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.080
Those who say they are wary

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.730
of taking the vaccine
cite different reasons.

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.040
According to a survey, 41% of people

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.470
who hadn't yet been vaccinated

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.810
said they feared side effects

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:07.070
and 30% said they weren't sure
the vaccine was effective.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:09.080
One issue health workers are focused on

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.820
is vaccine misinformation,
stressing to people

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.850
that vaccines have gone
through clinical trials

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.691
before being authorized
by local authorities.

00:02:16.691 --> 00:02:17.770
- People have a lot of fears

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:18.792
'cause they hear a bunch of things

00:02:18.792 --> 00:02:20.760
from different friends or
different news channels

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.310
that aren't necessarily true.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.900
- To help with that, we have volunteers

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.700
who are out and around
in the market explaining

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.139
to people the importance,
answering questions

00:02:28.139 --> 00:02:30.120
and actually bringing them here.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.510
- [Narrator] Some campaigns
focus on the ultra-orthodox

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.090
and Arab communities where
some have been skeptical

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.920
of the vaccination program.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.850
The government has also set up a taskforce

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.431
to fight vaccine misinformation,

00:02:40.431 --> 00:02:42.220
like these employees are doing here

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.700
in Israel's Health Ministry control room.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.206
And in some cases, it seems to be working.

00:02:47.206 --> 00:02:51.123
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.970
- [Narrator] In Holon, a
suburb south of Tel Aviv,

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.540
volunteers at this popup
clinic offer goodie bags

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.060
and free basketball tickets
to the first 5,000 people

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.370
to get vaccinated.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.830
- We're trying to do our best
to give the people the idea

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.170
to come and take the vaccine.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.380
- [Narrator] Around 85%
of Holon's residents

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.530
had already been vaccinated

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.410
at the beginning of March.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.780
One reason Israel is pushing
its vaccination program so hard

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.670
is that it's crucial to the country's plan

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.720
to reopen its economy quickly.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.180
- The fact that Israel has been so fast

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.530
in vaccinating it residents

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.380
also means we will probably be the fastest

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.100
in reopening our market.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.660
- [Narrator] Citizens
who have been inoculated

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.240
can register for Israel's
green pass system,

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.340
which is meant to help
the country reopen safely

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:40.950
and allow activities like
indoor dining to resume.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.460
- [Man] The green
passport essentially says

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.210
if you've been vaccinated twice,

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:46.420
you have access to all these places.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.640
- Some other countries,
including Saudi Arabia

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:51.300
and the EU have said they were
considering similar systems

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.800
for people who had gotten their vaccines.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.170
But critics have raised questions

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.720
on whether the strategy could result

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.200
in a two-speed system

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.890
with potentially unequal access

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.170
to some public services and travel.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.390
Israel says the system
isn't affecting access

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.302
to essential services.

00:04:06.302 --> 00:04:08.470
(upbeat music)

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:09.340
- For the first time,

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.251
we are allowed to have a rock concert

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.040
but the restrictions still apply.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.610
So only 500 people can attend this show.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:18.037
There are 30,000 seats and 500 people.

00:04:18.037 --> 00:04:19.930
- [Narrator] But green
passes are allowing people

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:22.410
to take cautious steps towards normalcy.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.410
- The green pass program is great.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.720
It feels like things
are starting to open up

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.708
and getting back to what
we were used to awhile ago.

00:04:29.708 --> 00:04:32.291
(upbeat music)

